WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.596 --> 00:00:11.747
Sign in as the platform admin.

2
00:00:11.847 --> 00:00:18.753
Plans are what you sell. Each has a monthly and a yearly price. The Trial plan is what new businesses start on.

3
00:00:18.853 --> 00:00:22.404
Click Edit on Starter to see what a plan controls.

4
00:00:22.504 --> 00:00:26.715
The name, code, currency, prices and the number of trial days.

5
00:00:26.815 --> 00:00:32.456
Limits cap branches, team members and products. Leave a limit empty and it is unlimited.

6
00:00:32.556 --> 00:00:38.362
The tick boxes switch features on or off for this plan, such as coupons, gift cards or SMS.

7
00:00:38.462 --> 00:00:42.233
We leave without saving. Cancel goes back to the list.

8
00:00:42.333 --> 00:00:48.196
Invoices lists every payment from every business, with its plan, amount, status and gateway.

9
00:00:48.296 --> 00:00:53.333
Tabs filter by status: pending, paid, failed or void. Here are the paid ones.

10
00:00:53.433 --> 00:00:59.214
You can also filter by gateway, by mode, by date, or search by business name.

11
00:00:59.314 --> 00:01:05.560
Manage opens one invoice. Void cancels it and can take back the days it added, so use it with care.

12
00:01:05.660 --> 00:01:11.300
Payments, under Settings, is where you connect the gateways your businesses pay through.

13
00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:17.151
Stripe, Razorpay, Flutterwave and PayPal each have an on or off switch and their own keys.

14
00:01:17.251 --> 00:01:23.496
Each gateway has a Live and a Test mode, and shows the webhook address to paste into its dashboard.

15
00:01:23.596 --> 00:01:30.006
Billing sets the grace period after a failed renewal, the reminder days and the invoice number prefix.

16
00:01:30.106 --> 00:01:35.746
That is plans and billing. Plans set what a business gets, invoices record what it paid.
